WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.690
It is known as the rainbow nation for its
cultural, linguistic and religious diversity.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.550
It’s constitution alone acknowledges 11
different languages!

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:25.710
Yes, this is South Africa, a country situated
in the extreme south of Africa.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.170
This is not a small country, its surface is
larger than Germany, France, Italy, Belgium

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.460
and the Netherlands combined!

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.520
It is, by far, the most developed economy
of all the countries situated south of the

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.660
Sahara desert.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:43.260
In the year 2010, it was the first African
country to hold a Soccer World Championship.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.270
The summer of Shakira´s “Waka Waka” if
anyone cares to remember that...

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:55.379
The most important month in South Africa’s
History was April 1994.

00:00:55.379 --> 00:01:01.020
Between the 26th and 29th of that month, South
Africa celebrated the first, free, universal,

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.519
and democratic elections.

00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:06.590
They were also the longest because the elections
last for 4 long days.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.460
During that time, South Africans left their
houses massively to vote... having to wait

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.740
in queues kilometers long!

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:21.540
The hype was justified, for these elections
meant the end of 300 years of colonialism

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.870
and white supremacy.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:28.710
The elections marked the end of apartheid.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:34.070
APARTHEID
Apartheid was a system based on racial segregation

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.000
which remained in effect for 50 years.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.710
It mainly consisted of separating the white
population from the black population.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:45.480
This applied in any situation: living, studying,
even the spending of leisure time.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.140
Obviously, as you might imagine, all the best
areas and services were built for, and used

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.140
by, the white population.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.200
A good example were ambulances.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.320
Even though the black population were 80%
of the total population, the barely had any

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.700
ambulances to use.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.780
However, the ambulances for the white population
were numerous and, also, refused to carry

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:15.500
black people because they couldn’t according
to the law.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.310
Apartheid gave the white population all the
political power and, also, established many

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.019
limitations, precisely, in order to consolidate
white power.

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:27.030
As an example, mixed race relationships and
marriage were completely forbidden.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:33.190
Quite simply, It left the black population
in an inhuman situation.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:39.709
It could be said there were two different
South Africa's, one black and terribly poor,

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:41.340
and the other, white, and very wealthy.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.349
And of course, those who rebelled suffered
terrible punishments and repression...

00:02:45.349 --> 00:03:10.329
MANDELA´S DREAM
But that 

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:15.310
all changed in 1994 thanks to Nelson Mandela,
also known as Madiba.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:19.560
He was considered the father of the country.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.709
Mandela lead the political fight against Apartheid
and racism, but he had to pay for it.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:27.420
In 1961 he was sentenced to life imprisonment
for betrayal.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.950
Mandela spent 27 years in jail, until 1992.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:37.109
Nevertheless, two years later in the 1994
elections were held and he was elected as

00:03:37.109 --> 00:03:45.189
President of South Africa, the first black
president in the country's history.

00:03:45.189 --> 00:03:49.260
Many were surprised to see Mandela aiming
for reconciliation rather than revenge.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.870
Mandela dreamt of a free, united, and prosperous
South Africa.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.569
He made it clear in his inaugural speech:
We have triumphed in the effort to implant

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:00.349
hope in the breasts of the millions of our
people.

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:05.989
We enter into a covenant that we shall build
the society in which all South Africans, both

00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:13.819
black and white, will be able to walk tall,
without any fear in their hearts, assured

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:19.079
of their inalienable right to human dignity
- a rainbow nation at peace with itself and

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:20.079
the world.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:21.079
Mandela kept his word.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:25.290
He worked towards a united South Africa, and
when the time came, he left power following

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.980
the limits of the constitution.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:34.390
This all turned him into a legend for the
country.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:39.410
But let’s now focus on present-day South
Africa.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:44.110
It is the only country in the world to hold
three capital cities: Cape Town, the capital

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:49.070
city for legislative power, Pretoria, for
executive power, and Bloemfontein, the judicial

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.070
capital city.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:54.570
And on top of that, neither is the the most
populated or the one where most businesses

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:55.570
concentrate…

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.410
For that we have to move to a fourth city:
Johannesburg.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:04.510
It’s not uncommon for different textbooks
to state different cities as the capital of

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.510
South Africa.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:09.920
Now, after the fall of Apartheid, South Africa
experienced quite an economic boost.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:19.380
Since 1994, the economy, considering purchasing
power, has tripled.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.000
Poverty has been strongly reduced and hundreds
of thousands of black families make it into

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.190
the middle class every year.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:30.340
And even though violence is still high (it
needs to be said that South Africa is quite

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.860
a violent country) it has also reduced.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:37.130
Further, in general, the access to drinkable
water, electricity and health care has also

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.440
improved quite a lot.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.780
To illustrate the situation: South Africa
is the biggest tourist center and financial

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.650
power in the south of the continent.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.830
Its stock market is the most important in
Africa and it is, also, an important place

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.510
for the automotive industry.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.580
Companies such as BMW and General Motors have
factories here.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.790
So it all sounds pretty good, right?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.810
Well, things today are actually not looking
that rosy.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:04.690
CRISIS AND STAGNATION
Despite its numerous achievements, the economy

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.390
hasn’t changed since 2009.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:10.210
The economy isn’t growing, unemployment
rates are one of the highest in the world

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.440
and, in general, very few people are working.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:17.780
The country has a population of about 55 million
people, 15 million are without work, and many

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:20.470
of these jobs that people do have are informal.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:23.080
And this is not the only problem.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.250
Investment by companies has also kept decreasing
in the last 9 years.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:30.690
Its currency, the RAND, has been greatly depreciated
and public debt is about to be declared as

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.840
"junk bonds".

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:34.440
This is a pretty major economic disaster.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.940
In fact, in the last years, people with money
are escaping the country.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:40.990
So what happened in South Africa?

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:44.090
What lead to this crisis?

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:50.670
JACOB ZUMA
This is Jacob Zuma, the president since 2009,

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:54.330
and his years in office have been, well, they’ve
been a huge mess.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:58.040
The man is facing 783 corruption cases.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:10.580
He been described as a professional at taking
things that are not his.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:20.940
But this is not the only issue.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.620
Mr. Zuma´s political decisions don’t encourage
foreign investment.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:28.050
Further, the President's labor regulations
are an obstacle when it comes to job creation.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.580
And the regulations are getting more and more
rigid.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.650
His last idea was a huge raise in minimum
wage.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:37.080
Something that doesn’t make a bunch of sense
in a country where there are so few people

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.080
working.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:42.160
In fact, many financial analysts have criticized
the measure by saying it is nonsensical to

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.490
establish a minimum wage which amounts to
twice as much as half of the workers are making.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:51.530
Now, let’s be honest, we all want our salaries
to raise, but to do so we´ll need to create

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.530
wealth first, don't you think?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.361
If job creation was already an issue before,
imagine what’s going to happen now with

00:07:56.361 --> 00:07:57.940
higher salaries.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:59.530
South Africa has other problems too.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:05.190
An important one is its problematic education
system...

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:13.900
AN AWFUL EDUCATION SYSTEM
The education system in South Africa is pretty

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.770
awful:
Picture this: 1 in every 3 students who has

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:21.120
attended school for 6 years has difficulties
when it comes to something as essential as

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:26.270
reading, and only 1 in every 100 black students
gets an engineering diploma.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.800
We can now understand the reason why national
companies complain about the difficulty to

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.990
find skilled labour.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.839
And it is not a money issue.

00:08:32.839 --> 00:08:42.740
South Africa is one of the countries with
a highest investment in education in the world.

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:44.330
So, what’s happening?

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.269
According to some people, the ones to blame
are the Democratic Teachers´ Union.

00:08:48.269 --> 00:08:52.209
They control the state education system and
it has become a real mafia.

00:08:52.209 --> 00:08:54.149
The Union is an ally of President Zuma.

00:08:54.149 --> 00:08:58.310
Zuma, besides putting an end to education
supervision, he has pulled so many strings

00:08:58.310 --> 00:09:03.079
get more teachers that the education level
of teachers themselves is very low.

00:09:03.079 --> 00:09:07.959
A few years ago, maths teachers in the country
were given a test (these were teachers teaching

00:09:07.959 --> 00:09:10.069
maths to 11 and 12 year-olds.)

00:09:10.069 --> 00:09:11.069
The result?

00:09:11.069 --> 00:09:15.980
8 out of 10 of these teachers got lower results
than the the results expected of their students.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:35.740
And to be honest, maths isn’t exactly of
the President´s strengths...

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:43.240
Obviously, the results in white students,
who go to private schools, are far better.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:52.639
Showing that maybe some of that apartheid
heritage is still in effect…

00:09:52.639 --> 00:09:57.009
If these problems weren’t bad enough, racial
conflict in South Africa has been growing

00:09:57.009 --> 00:09:58.170
in the last few years.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:02.779
The Economic Freedom Fighters is a radical
political party founded in 2013.

00:10:02.779 --> 00:10:06.110
This party is now the third largest political
force in the country.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:10.410
Some if its members are suggesting to almost
invert Apartheid and apply it to the white

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:11.410
population.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.420
It is still a minority party but as an element
of subversion it works quite well.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.980
Anyway, it looks like Mandela's dream is now
in danger.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:21.490
So, what do you think?

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:25.379
Will South Africa make Madiba´s dreams come
true?

00:10:25.379 --> 00:10:27.910
Will South Africa become the most prosperous
nation in Africa again?

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.470
Or will hatred, distrust, and bad politics
triumph?

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:32.899
